# MongoDB Atlas support

**Area:** `db.py`, `settings.py`
**Roadmap:** [02-deploy](../roadmap/02-deploy.md)
**Depends on:** #26 (environment config)

## Goal

Make the database connection work with MongoDB Atlas so we can use a hosted database in production.

## Work

### Remove `directConnection=true`

- In `db.py`, remove `directConnection=true` from the connection string — this parameter prevents connecting to Atlas replica sets

### Use `MONGODB_URI` environment variable

- The connection string should come from `settings.py` via `MONGODB_URI` (Atlas provides a full URI including credentials)
- Default to `mongodb://localhost:27017/maestro` for local development

### Verify Atlas compatibility

- Ensure Beanie/Motor works with Atlas connection strings (SRV format: `mongodb+srv://...`)
- Test that all document operations work against Atlas

## Tests

- Integration tests continue to work with mongomock (no change)
- Manual: connect to Atlas free tier and run the app

## Notes

- Atlas free tier provides 512MB on a shared cluster — sufficient to start.
- The Atlas URI includes authentication, so no separate username/password settings needed.
